    "raw": "{\n  \"entity_id\": \"9abbd30b40007f1f85aeb09a2b5bd3e41285e276683f57f6222e003a59f9228f\",\n  \"attributes\": [\n    {\n      \"attribute\": \"legal.verdict\",\n      \"status\": \"found\",\n      \"raw_value\": \"dismissed with costs\",\n      \"normalized_value\": \"Guilty\",\n      \"unit\": null,\n      \"period\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"source_id\": \"32.txt:c14\",\n          \"exact_span\": \"25 and s 425A are to be read together and s 425A does not impose a separate obligation to that in s 425. The process described in s 425A is the mechanism by which the invitation referred to in s 425 is to be issued ( VNAA v Minister for Immigration and Multicultural and Indigenous Affairs [2004] FCAFC 134 ; (2004) 136 FCR 407 at 413; Minister for Immigration and Multicultural and Indigenous Affairs v SZFHC [2006] FCAFC 73 ; (2006) 231 ALR 630). It follows, therefore, that the appeal is dismissed with costs.\"",
